Go to definition (IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN §8.4 Features, CLI.md §4): from a use to its declaration
(a field named in a literal, a type, a let named by a ref type), and from the key of a ref,
a string or a name, to the entry, here in a loaded JSON file that is not open. Every position
on the last line follows "/* é中😀 */ ", 11 UTF-16 units and 14 bytes (§8.4 Positions). A
built-in has no declaration: null.
-- proj/project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- proj/a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// An item.
record Item {
  /// Its name.
  name: String
}

/// Items, loaded.
let items: table Item = load("items.json")

/// A drop.
record Drop {
  /// What drops.
  item: ref items
}

/// Drops.
/* é中😀 */ let drops: [Drop] = [{ item: "sword" }, { item: shield }]
-- proj/a/items.json --
{
  "sword": { "name": "Sword" },
  "shield": { "name": "Shield" }
}
